# Line endings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under this image runs on Linux. With core.autocrlf=true (the
# Windows default) git checks text files out as CRLF, and a CRLF script that
# is *executed directly* dies with:
#     /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
# because the shebang picks up the carriage return.
#
# entrypoint.sh is invoked as the container ENTRYPOINT, so it MUST stay LF on
# every platform. Python files are safer (CPython accepts CRLF) but are pinned
# to LF as well so a build context copied straight off a Windows box behaves
# exactly like one produced by a Linux checkout.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sh        text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Compose / yaml are only parsed, never executed - let git decide.
*.yml       text
*.yaml      text

# Never let git mangle binaries.
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.exe       binary
*.msi       binary
*.zip       binary
